# Code owners.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the matching owner(s) on any PR touching these
# paths. Branch protection on main pairs this with:
#   require_code_owner_reviews: true
#   required_approving_review_count: 0
# which means: no review is required by default, but a PR touching a path
# below CANNOT merge until an owner of that path (other than the PR's own
# author) has approved. A lane owner working only inside their own lane needs
# no approval — the only listed owner IS the author, so there's no one else
# for the rule to require. Touch a path outside your lane and you need that
# lane's owner to approve. Later patterns take precedence over earlier ones —
# see https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners/
#
# Lawrecesss (Lin Htet Shein) owns data/metrics and is the catch-all default
# for anything not claimed by a more specific lane below (root config, shared
# top-level docs, etc.) — not a co-owner of the other three lanes, so their
# self-contained PRs don't need his approval either.

# Default owner for anything not matched more specifically below.
